  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 12-layer alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 antireflection stack on silicon substrate for normal-incidence unpolarized illumination. Initialize all layer thicknesses using quarter-wave optical thickness formula d = lambda_0/(4*n) where lambda_0 = 1380 nm (weighted center between 1260-1360 nm and 1530-1565 nm bands), then explicitly project all thicknesses to be >= 80 nm before optimization begins. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with step-size multiplier reduced to 0.5x compared to standard settings. Optimize for mean transmittance across both wavelength bands [1260-1360 nm, 1530-1565 nm]. Layer sequence: Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2 (12 finite layers total). Thickness bounds: 20-400 nm per layer. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 1260-1360 nm, 1530-1565 nm. soft objectives: low average reflectance in 1260-1360 nm band; low average reflectance in 1530-1565 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflection in the specified bands. manufacturing constraints: maximum 12 layers; individual layer thickness between 20 nm and 400 nm; materials restricted to Ta2O5 and SiO2.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a 12-layer alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 antireflection coating on a silicon substrate under normal-incidence unpolarized illumination. Initialize all layer thicknesses using the quarter-wave formula at 1380 nm and enforce a minimum of 80 nm. Bounds are 20–400 nm per layer. Use a gradient-based optimizer with halved step size to minimize mean reflectance across the 1260–1360 nm and 1530–1565 nm bands simultaneously.",
